<StaticPage path="/how-we-make-money/" h1="How Opus Calculator makes money" updated="2026-11-23">
  <p class="mt-6">The short version: the site is free, and it is paid for by one advertisement on each page. That is the only way it earns money.</p>

  <h2>One ad per page</h2>
  <p>
    Each page has a single advertising slot. It sits below the calculator and its explanation of the result, never above the fold, so you see and can use the
    calculator before any ad. The slot is reserved at a fixed size, so nothing on the page jumps around when an ad loads, and the ad only loads after the
    calculator is ready to use.
  </p>

  <h2>Ads never affect the calculation</h2>
  <p>
    A calculator's result depends only on the numbers you type and the formula shown on the page. The ad system is separate and cannot read your inputs or
    change an output. We do not rank, order or write calculators to suit an advertiser, and an advertiser cannot pay for a calculator to say anything. Read the
    <a href="/ad-disclosure/">ad disclosure</a> for the plain-language version.
  </p>

  <h2>What we do not do</h2>
  <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
    <li>
      We do not sell your data. The site collects almost none: see the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.
    </li>
    <li>We do not charge for any calculator, hide a result behind a sign-up, or ask for an email address.</li>
    <li>We do not take payment for a favourable mention of a lender, broker, clinic or product.</li>
    <li>We do not present a calculator as financial, medical or legal advice. The disclaimers under the results say so.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Where the money goes</h2>
  <p>Advertising income pays for hosting, the domain name, the tools used to test the calculators, and the time it takes to keep the formulas correct.</p>

  <h2>If the model changes</h2>
  <p>If the site ever adds another source of income, this page and the ad disclosure will say so before it starts, and the calculators will stay free.</p>
</StaticPage>
